! mcp_bootstrap_p2.strap -- MCP's IPL BOOTSTRAP, printed page 2.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.9, header "PAGE NUMBER 2", banner
! "MCP INIALIZATION BOOTSTRAP" (IBM's own spelling, kept).
!
! THE FIRST PAGE OF IBM's OPERATING SYSTEM IN THIS CORPUS.
! docs/boot_plan.md M3.  Sixteen rows carry printed machine code and
! every one of them is checked by verify_mcp_bootstrap_p2.py --
! AGENTS.md rule 3, against the listing's own BINARY OUTPUT column.
!
! WHAT THIS PAGE IS.  Lines 15-39 are the first fragment of the
! routine the IPL hardware loads: it plants the IPL control word,
! clears the lower registers and the indicators, then sizes core
! storage by clearing it until an address-invalid interruption says
! where the top is.  Reference Manual printed p.126's sequence --
! which strap/programs/ipl_boot.strap already exercises end to end --
! is what puts it in memory and starts it at X IPL BS.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS, all four of them
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED.  The listing prints
!     "X IPL BS", "X BS END", "XW SR", "X CL IND", "X S ROOF".
!     C22-6531 printed p.10 limits a symbol to "six or fewer
!     alphabetic and numeric characters" and requires it to contain
!     "only alphameric characters", and every one of these is exactly
!     six or fewer once the blanks come out -- see docs/NEXT.md 5t,
!     where fifteen of them are checked.  So XIPLBS, XBSEND, XWSR,
!     XCLIND, XSROOF.
!
! (2) THE LISTING-CONTROL PSEUDO-OPS OF LINES 3-9 ARE OMITTED, not
!     translated: PUNFUL, PUNORG, PUNID, RESEQ, PRNS.  strap_asm.py
!     accepts them (LISTING_CONTROL) and they emit nothing, so their
!     presence or absence cannot move a bit.  They are left out
!     because this file is the bootstrap, not the deck that punched
!     it.
!
! (3) LINE 10's "TAIL,(2)G" IS OMITTED.  C28-6129 printed p.37: TAIL
!     "appends the symbol that appears in its address field as a tail
!     to every symbol in the statements that follow".  It is suffix
!     mangling for assembling separate programs together, and with
!     one tail covering the whole program every definition and every
!     reference is mangled alike -- so a standalone assembly is
!     bit-identical with or without it (docs/NEXT.md 5x).  strap_asm
!     does not implement it and deliberately refuses it rather than
!     ignoring it silently; omitting it here is the honest form.
!
! (4) LINE 27's "(A*)DD(BU,32,8),C911*" IS A ZERO OF THE SAME WIDTH.
!     C28-6129 printed p.16: "(A*)" is the A entry mode -- IBM BCD --
!     with "*" as the end-of-statement character, so the datum is the
!     four characters C911.  strap_asm has no BCD table yet (that is
!     Appendix C, printed pp.47-53).  THE LISTING PRINTS NO MACHINE
!     CODE FOR THIS ROW, and its own comment calls it a "SLOT FOR
!     DATE OF SOURCE TAPE", i.e. a placeholder patched at run time.
!     DD(BU,32,8),0 occupies the identical 32 bits, so every later
!     address still lands where the listing says -- which the sixteen
!     checked rows prove, since X BEGIN at 000043.40 follows it.
!     NOTHING IS CHECKED ABOUT ITS CONTENT and nothing may be.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- SYN'd at the addresses other pages print for them.
! EVERY SYN IS AN INPUT TO THE CHECK, NOT A WITNESS: a SYN makes its
! own address come out right by construction, so these rows prove
! only that every OTHER field lands where the listing puts it.
! XW SR and X S ROOF are defined on printed p.13 ("BOOTSTRAP
! DEFINITIONS"); X BS END on printed p.14, the last line of the
! PROSA control-word table, as "- END OF THE MCP IPL BS ROUTINE".
XWSR    SYN, (8)547.0      ! p.13: "X WS R  XW,0.0,29,XW IND"
XSROOF  SYN, (8)546.0      ! p.13: "X S ROOF  XW,0  -TEMP STORE FOR SIZE"
XBSEND  SYN, (8)621.0      ! p.14: "X BS END  SYN,$"

        SLC, (8)40.0       ! line 15

! ---- the IPL control word the hardware refills from location 4 ----
! Reference Manual printed p.126: the fixed control word reads ONE
! word into location 4, "its refill address causes the next control
! word to be fetched from location 4", and THIS is that word.  Count
! is the whole bootstrap, X BS END - X IPL BS = 0o560 = 368 words.
! "ONE IN REFILL FIELD IDENTIFIES IPLCW" -- printed p.3 finds which
! channel IPL'd by scanning for that bit.
        CW(CR), XIPLBS, XBSEND-XIPLBS, 1       ! line 17

! ---- the bootstrap proper -----------------------------------------
XIPLBS  BD,  XBEGIN        ! line 24  -DISABLE AND START IPL.  p.126
                            ! requires the first instruction loaded by
                            ! IPL to be BRANCH DISABLED.
        VF,  0             ! line 25  -SLOT FOR TAPE CW
        XW,  0             ! line 26  -SLOT FOR DISK CW
XVERFY  DD(BU,32,8), 0     ! line 27  -SLOT FOR DATE OF SOURCE TAPE
                            ! IN A-8.  See substitution (4).
XBEGIN  LX,  $X15, XWSR    ! line 28  - INITIALIZE TO CLEAR LOWER REGISTERS
        Z,   0.0           ! line 29
XLOOP   Z,   2.0($X15)     ! line 30  -CLEAR LOWER REGESTERS (sic)
        CBR+, $X15, XLOOP  ! line 31
        L(BU), XWSR+.32    ! line 32  -DONE CLEAR C AND D REGISTERS
XCLIND  BMKZ, $+.32        ! line 33
        M+1(BU,6), XCLIND+.19   ! line 34 -CLEAR NON MASKABLE INDIC AND
                            ! "M+1", DIGIT ONE, NOT "M+I".  Read at 600
                            ! dpi: the glyph has a digit's angled top
                            ! flag and matches the 1 in "$+1.0" two rows
                            ! below, while the I in "IND" on this very
                            ! row carries top and bottom serifs.  This
                            ! is docs/listing_typography.md's letter-I
                            ! vs digit-1 trap in the REVERSE direction
                            ! from how it is usually hit.
                            !
                            ! And the semantics confirm the glyph: M+1
                            ! adds ONE to the 6-bit field at
                            ! X CL IND+.19, which is the mask-bit number
                            ! inside the BMKZ at 000046.40 -- the
                            ! instruction steps that number through the
                            ! non-maskable indicators, exactly what the
                            ! comment says.  M+I would have made the
                            ! operand an immediate datum instead of an
                            ! address, which is why the first attempt
                            ! put 0o63 at bit 18 of the address field.
        CB,  $X15, XCLIND  ! line 35
XCLSTO  Z,   0.0($X15)     ! line 36  -CLEAR ONE WORD
        BADZ, $+1.0        ! line 37  -IF DONE CLEARING STORAGE
        CB+, $X15, XCLSTO  ! line 38  -ADVANCE AND RETURN
        SV,  $X15, XSROOF  ! line 39  -TEMPORARILY SAVE 7030 SIZE
        END, XIPLBS
